, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Prodigy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "kz", "country_name": "Kazakhstan", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Limp Bizkit", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Marilyn Manson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rammstein", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Hot Chili Peppers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "new wave": {"genre": "new wave", "country_code": "kz", "country_name": "Kazakhstan", "summary": "New wave is today a quite broad umbrella term describing popular music from around 1977 to 1986. But originally it was a slim sub genre of Western popular music that arose in the United Kingdom about 1977-78. It had close ties to punk rock and fairly strong influences of the musical style that had been invented and continuously developed throughout the 1970s: reggae.\n\nThe term new wave was first a kind of description of a mo